AXIS-1024 Optimized Implementation

This directory contains the AXIS-1024 implementation for mainstream 64-bit PC
software builds. It preserves the ICCS CryptHash API and can be built with the
included Makefile.

The current optimized code uses the common AXIS core in axis_core.c. For
AXIS-1024, the public CryptHash path routes byte-aligned messages through the
validated SoA fast path. AVX2 builds use the 8x32-bit SoA block, while portable
builds use the scalar SoA block; both preserve the one-bit-per-beat absorption
rule of the reference implementation.
For byte-aligned pure message blocks, the AVX2 path uses the same-message
kernel because the two message inputs are identical at every beat.

Optimization levels are selected at compile time with AXIS_OPT_LEVEL:
- 1: portable optimized, no AVX2/BMI2/native intrinsics.
- 2: AVX2 optimized, no BMI2/native tuning.
- 3: best available, enables native target tuning and BMI2 when available.

The Makefile exposes the same levels as `make portable`, `make avx2`, and
`make best`; plain `make` defaults to best available.
The optimized build configurations are kept for reproducible portable, AVX2,
and best-available builds, while correctness for AXIS-1024 is checked against
the same known-answer test vectors as the reference implementation.
